@page "/help"

<PageTitle>Help</PageTitle>

<main class="help-page">
    <section class="help-hero">
        <h1>LocalGPT Help</h1>
        <p>Use LocalGPT as a local AI workbench for Ollama, DXAiChat memory, and Minecraft Java mod building.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-grid">
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>Setup</h2>
            <p>Open Install, discover Ollama or LM Studio, select the model, and save the configuration. For local debugging, prefer Ollama with gpt-oss:20b.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>Chat Memory</h2>
            <p>DXAiChat auto-saves completed messages into SQLite. Use Save Memory before closing, Recall Latest to continue, or the memory selector to reopen older chats and former model thoughts.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>AI Council</h2>
            <p>Select two or more Ollama models to propose, critique, verify, and save a shared transcript. If a model is missing or the request sounds blocked, the council asks for a user decision poll.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>Minecraft Builder</h2>
            <p>Use Minecraft Mod Builder for Fabric-style workspace planning, buildable file paths, Gradle commands, and scoped native command execution.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>Formatting</h2>
            <p>gpt-oss responses are cleaned before display so Harmony channel markers do not leak into the chat. Thinking appears in a collapsible section above the final answer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="help-panel">
            <h2>Grounded Reviews</h2>
            <p>Use gpt-oss as a second reviewer with supplied facts only. Unsupported suggestions belong under Needs verification before they influence code or setup steps.</p>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="help-panel help-wide">
        <h2>Good Minecraft Prompt Shape</h2>
        <p>Start with the project goal, list required systems in order, name the critical path, and ask for file paths, scoreboard/storage design, commands, and performance notes.</p>
    </section>
</main>
